  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Suppose $a,b,c$ are positive numbers and $c\\ne1$. Prove that\n$$\\log_c(a+b)=\\log_c a+\\log_c b+\\log_c\\left(\\frac{a+b}{ab}\\right).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\log_c a+\\log_c b+\\log_c\\left(\\frac{a+b}{ab}\\right)=\\log_c\\left(ab\\cdot\\frac{a+b}{ab}\\right)=\\log_c(a+b)$.\n\nUse the product law to combine the three logarithms.",
      "worked": "Using the product law:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_c(a+b)&=\\log_c\\left(a\\left(1+\\frac ba\\right)\\right)\\\\\\log_c(a+b)&=\\log_c a+\\log_c\\left(1+\\frac ba\\right)\\\\\\log_c(a+b)&=\\log_c a+\\log_c b+\\log_c\\left(\\frac1b+\\frac1a\\right)\\\\\\log_c(a+b)&=\\log_c a+\\log_c b+\\log_c\\left(\\frac{a+b}{ab}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
